## Remaining work

### `/aide:brain` Mode 2 shim refactor

Gut the default mode in `.claude/commands/aide/brain.md` to a 3-line shim:
"call `aide_brain`, branch on `backend === null`, follow `instructions`."
Drop all Obsidian-specific prose. Mode 1 (`config`) stays Obsidian-only —
provisioning is a separate concern. Lives in a different module governed by
`.claude/.aide`; needs its own `/aide:plan` round.

### Agent frontmatter sweep — `mcpServers: [brain]`

Every agent definition under `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/` that
declares `mcpServers: [obsidian]` becomes `mcpServers: [brain]`. Bulk rewrite,
one-time. Must follow `aide_brain` shipping (already done) — agents must keep
working during the transition. Track as a separate task; consider as part of
a broader "agent definitions audit."

Also sweep prose-level references to `mcp__obsidian__*` tool names in agent
prose / skill descriptions / command files. The prose now uses
`mcp__brain__*` (per the fixed-key decision); existing references are stale.

### Obsidian orphan-key cleanup

`provisionBrain.buildBrainMcpStep` emits `would-overwrite` when both `brain`
and `obsidian` keys are present, but does NOT delete the `obsidian` orphan.
A follow-up plan removes the `obsidian` key from `mcpServers` after the
`brain` write succeeds. Holding for a separate plan keeps the migration step's
scope tight (one write, one prescription) and avoids interleaving
delete-on-overwrite logic into `applySteps`.

### `aide_info` description update

Today `aide_info`'s description in `src/index.ts` says nothing about
`aide_brain`. A one-line addition ("for runtime brain reach prose, call
`aide_brain` on demand") helps agents that read only the tool list at
handshake time. Not a blocker — agents learn about `aide_brain` from its
own description.

### Stale handoff/spec references to old `buildBrainState` location

The lift moved `buildBrainState` from `src/tools/info/buildBrainState/` to
`src/service/buildBrainState/`. Some `.aide` and plan files still reference
the old path historically (acceptable as point-in-time intent records), but
ONE non-historical reference exists:

- This file's prior version had a "current backend detection" line pointing
  at the old path. Already corrected in this rewrite, but worth grepping for
  any other "current" framing of the old path before next session.

### `config.aide` — host-project configuration (still deferred)

Not a blocker. Becomes load-bearing once we ship a second backend (need a
tiebreaker between two `brain`-shaped wirings) or once we want configuration
explicit and version-controlled instead of inferred.

Open design questions before scoping:

- **Scope** — brain-only, or AIDE-wide (IDE choice, framework override, etc.)?
- **Format** — real `.aide` spec (with intent + outcomes), or `.aide/config.yaml`
  (config is user choice, not module intent)? Leaning toward yaml.
- **Migration** — existing installs have no config file; need a fallback
  inference path so they keep working.

### `provisionBrain` modernization (deferred)

Currently writes an Obsidian-shaped vault `CLAUDE.md` template with
`mcp__obsidian__*` references baked in. Now stale (the prose should reference
`mcp__brain__*` since the MCP key is fixed at `brain`). Will need to be
backend-aware once a second backend lands. **Higher priority than originally
flagged** because of the fixed-`brain`-key shift — even before a second
backend, the seeded prose is wrong about tool names.

